<h1>North-South Handy (Eskimo Tune/Sweet Richard)</h1>
<h6>©Trad, Greenland and the Southern United States</h6>

<p>        <i>I learned "Sweet Richard" from
Tom Judge and Nick Apollonio, of
Tenant's Harbor, Maine. Tom called
it "a southern tune." The Eskimo
tune is about as far from that as
you can get: it was collected in
Greenland around the turn of the
century, where some Eskimos were
dancing to it. The chords are my
own. (GB)</i>

</p>

